*Heading
abq2ccx validation: the reaction force at a *RIGID BODY reference node that is one of the
body's own nodes.  ccx 2.23 prints the reaction at such a node as its own elements' forces
alone (about 1e-15 for a rigid body); abq2ccx gives the body a free reference node at the
same place, which carries the BCs and output requests the deck gives the node.
Three unit cubes (C3D8, E = 1000), each held at its bottom face, with a rigid unit cube on
top, pushed down 0.01 through a frictionless node-to-surface HARD contact (NLGEOM):
 A: *Rigid Body, PIN NSET = the rigid cube's nodes, REF NODE = its top corner node 18;
 B: *Rigid Body, ELSET = the rigid cube, REF NODE = its top corner node 118;
 R: *Rigid Body, PIN NSET = the rigid cube's nodes, REF NODE = free node 299 (the control).
The reference node's RF3 must balance the supports' total, and A, B and R must agree.
